{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head `53aac7cdbafc9966305823231c05579ebddcabbf`, as a true record of the run. The scene passed on the deployed Worker, driven by scripts, with no person and no desktop AI app. One stop in that scene stays unexplained, and I read it as a possible product fault, so it needs an owner. See below.\n\n**The two attempts.** I read both, and I do not think the timeout is a flaw in the script or the network that can be set aside.\n\n- `failed-read-1/browser-requests-through-stop.ndjson` shows the row press drew the right issue's reads, in the same order as the later runs, and every one with a status answered 200. The six rows with no status are not at issue here: the last ones are a font and a read that also appear in passing traces.\n- The trace reaches the lane's `/stream` and one summary after it. In `drawWorkbench`, `observeView` runs after `panelFor` has filled the slots, and `showRoom` follows it. So the draw reached the end of the issue branch with all its data.\n- The script then waited 60 s for `[data-action-slot=\"comment\"]` to be visible, with no further request. That `div` has no size until `panelFor`'s `tasks` appends the form, so an empty slot and a screen that was never published look the same to this wait.\n- The stop leaves no screenshot and no DOM, so the record cannot tell which it was. `showFor` drops a draw whose number is no longer current, and a later draw that returned early would leave the list on screen. Or `tasks` left the slot empty, and the same callback places Approve and Decide. Either one matters to a person: they would press a row and see no issue, or an issue with no way to answer.\n- The diagnostic and the passing runs came from a new page load. They show that the path can pass, and not that it always does.\n\nSo I count one stop among the row presses of this unit, on a real Worker, cause unproved. The note says this plainly and claims no fix, which is the right record. **The planner decides whether J5 closes with that open. I recommend closing J5 on this record only with a named request:** make the script capture the screen and the DOM at a stop, then repeat the row press on a local Worker until it fails or a stated count passes.\n\n**What holds.**\n\n- **The unit.** `~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-01-j5-page-acceptance/` verifies against `SHA256SUMS` `12dc8743…`, and its 162 files hold none writable. My own scan for link, bearer and JWT shapes finds nothing in the text files. I read one screenshot, and it shows no link.\n- **The version.** `0-deployment.json` holds `samePageJs` true, with one digest for the frozen checkout and the deployed `page.js`, on version `300fb93a`.\n- **The clause that failed before.** `4-roomwide-read.json` has 51 steps and 0 failures. `after-reload.png` shows three rows across issues 3 and 4 with the rule and the settling act, and Rita's decision. The first device's rows are items 3, 5 and 8, with no omission.\n- **The control.** `4-roomwide-old-page.json` fails 15 of 19, first on \"the first screen lists what needs Ana across the room\", and it sent no act.\n- **The acts.** Each press has one `/acts` POST answering 200. The wait exits 0 after 535.958 s, 3950 ms after the Decide press. By `8-decide.json`, the POST left 2.4 s after the press, so most of that delay comes before the act. A fresh process signs entry 12. `dap verify` says `Result: consistent` and states that 10 other rooms' creation results stand on the service's word.\n- **After the acts.** `11-roomwide-after.json` has 43 steps and 0 failures, and the first device returns items 3 and 8.\n- **The earlier note's count.** It now says 78 hashed files plus `SHA256SUMS`, which answers `c75de866`.\n\nThis head changes three documentation paths, so it needs no gate. `check-notes`, `check-doc-links` (1006 links, 0 broken) and `check-commit-messages` pass, and the worktree is clean.\n\n**Limits the record names, and I confirm.** The deployed Page is `d56394da`, so it shows the digest in its rule lines; the card findings at `ce42f582` are not yet deployed. This room uses the Brief definition, so the default-room limit stays with `e82c6550`, and with it the issue screen's dependence on the decided query. The cut-list behaviour has only the local witness, because this room has four lanes.\n\n**Architecture.** A record, with no boundary change. The scene uses the real `apps/views` server, the deployed Page and the real wait.\n\n**Security.** The browser typed only the device link, and the evidence holds no token. Keys stay in place for a scratch room.\n\n**Simplification.** One note and one manifest, with nothing to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eb7241ed064d897054d3f9af97e3ed535e704fb3","binding":"assigned","head":"53aac7cdbafc9966305823231c05579ebddcabbf","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f4a4aa59eeecb0c9241efcb6faafce4bf1567f25\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d63500549fcca74a180b5389537151764a45341b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:627dd5ffc7363faac8bad02e69ed03075d2ac22a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}